<title>SRI LANKA: Dipped Products down on profit-taking.</title>
<headline>Dipped Products down on profit-taking.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dipped Products Ltd fell 5.8 percent or five rupees to 80 on turnover of 6,400 shares as a retail investor took profits, brokers said.</p>
<p>&quot;A small investor who bought the share at a much lower level is booking a little profit,&quot; said a broker.</p>
<p>Dipped Products manufactures industrial rubber gloves mainly for export.</p>
<p>-- Colombo newsroom (941) 434319</p>
</text>
